\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Love of God, how strong and true;
\par Eternal, and yet ever new;
\par Uncomprehended and unbought,
\par Beyond all knowledge and all thought!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O heavenly Love, how precious still,
\par In days of weariness and ill,
\par In nights of pain and helplessness,
\par To heal, to comfort, and to bless.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O wide-embracing, wondrous Love;
\par We read thee in the sky above,
\par We read thee in the earth below,
\par In seas that swell and streams that flow.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. We read thee best in Him who came
\par To bear for us the Cross of shame,
\par Sent by the Father from on high,
\par Our life to live, our death to die.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. We read thy power to bless and save
\par E'en in the darkness of the grave;
\par Still more in ressurection light
\par We read the fullness of thy might.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. O Love of God, our shield and stay
\par Through all the perils of our way;
\par Eternal Love, in thee we rest,
\par For ever safe, for ever blest.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

